<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="131" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>H8: Graph containerTypes port (ClientCertificateCredential, T6 cert from KV)</title>
    <phase>C'' Wave G-3 -- Identity + deploy</phase>
    <gate>blocked</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>T6 trap owner (SPE confidential-client creation) -- security-sensitive cert-based app-only auth. FULL rigor.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Well-specified Graph SDK port with a documented certificate-auth requirement (confidential-client per this project's MUST rules) -- Sonnet @ high.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>102, 103, 125, 126</deps>
    <tags>l2-controlplane, job-handler, option-d, sdk-port, auth</tags>
    <estimated-effort>8-12 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Port H8SpeContainerTypeHandler.cs's 3 collaborators: (1) CreateNewContainerTypeScriptProvisioner (Create-NewContainerType.ps1, 299 lines: az ad app x3, az keyvault secret x2 + container-type creation) -&gt; Microsoft.Graph POST /storage/fileStorage/containerTypes (fileStorageContainerType, Graph v1.0) under ClientCertificateCredential (T6 cert from KV -- CONFIDENTIAL CLIENT, per this project's MUST rule: 'MUST use confidential-client [app-only] token for SPE container-type creation [T6]'); app-reg reads via Graph Applications; (2) SpeContainerAppOnlyVerifier (Get-SpeContainerMetadata-AppOnly.ps1, 123 lines of token ceremony around ONE GET) -&gt; ClientCertificateCredential + Graph GET, dramatically simplified; (3) AzCliSpeContainerIdKvWriter (keyvault secret set/show, AzCliSpeContainerIdKvWriter.cs:85-108) -&gt; SecretClient (reuse task 125's KV writer pattern).</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Microsoft Graph fileStorageContainerType (SPE) provisioning under ClientCertificateCredential app-only auth, and canonical KV secret naming for the SPE-ContainerTypeId entry.</role>

  <goal>H8SpeContainerTypeHandler.cs's 3 collaborators are pure .NET SDK implementations. Container-type creation and the app-only metadata verify BOTH use ClientCertificateCredential (never a client-secret credential -- T6's whole point is confidential-client via certificate). The canonical SPE-ContainerTypeId KV name (per this project's naming remediation, Phase B task 011) is preserved.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>DS-1b §1 (H8 row) confirms the Graph SDK mapping for all 3 collaborators, with collaborator #17 (the verifier) noted as '123 lines of token ceremony around ONE GET' -- a strong simplification opportunity. This project's own Phase B (task 011, already ✅) already hardened the SOURCE SCRIPTS to confidential-client cert auth for T6 -- this task ports that ALREADY-CORRECT auth model to the SDK, it does not re-derive the T6 fix from scratch.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/SpeContainerType/H8SpeContainerTypeHandler.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/SpeContainerType/GraphContainerTypeProvisioner.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/SpeContainerType/GraphAppOnlyContainerVerifier.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">scripts/Create-NewContainerType.ps1</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">scripts/Get-SpeContainerMetadata-AppOnly.ps1</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="102" status="pending">wave-sequencing</dependency>
      <dependency task="103" status="pending">H8 keyed registration</dependency>
      <dependency task="125" status="pending">H4's SecretClient collaborator this task reuses for the KV writer</dependency>
      <dependency task="126" status="pending">H4's real-value-sourcing fix -- the cert secret H8 reads must be functional</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="design.md §4.1b">Handler runtime classification (Option D hybrid, DS-1b Sec.2): 12 handlers are pure .NET SDK/REST under DefaultAzureCredential pinned to the L2 UAMI (Class A); H14a is the sole Class-C residual (Exchange sidecar); H7/H10/H11/H12c are already native. No ProcessStartInfo/shell-out collaborator may remain in this handler's target state.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md MUST rules (post-line-254 block)">No new ProcessStartInfo/shell-out collaborator may be introduced by this task. Option D's entire point is deleting the pwsh/az/pac dependency from the L2 runtime, not adding to it (the sole designed exception is the H14a Exchange sidecar).</constraint>
    <constraint source="this project's CLAUDE.md MUST rules">MUST use confidential-client (app-only) token for SPE container-type creation (T6) -- ClientCertificateCredential, NEVER a client-secret-based credential for this specific operation.</constraint>
    <constraint source="DS-4 §2 H8 row">The 24h SPE replication gate (WaitingOnGate, session-free wait) is a RUN-LEVEL external blocker, not a handler defect -- do not attempt to poll around it faster or treat a pending-replication response as a handler failure.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>H8 Graph containerTypes port (T6 confidential-client)</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/design.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/design-study-ds4-handler-audit.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/design-study-ds4-handler-audit.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/design-study-ds1b-option-d-hybrid-deep-dive.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL). Read Create-NewContainerType.ps1 + Get-SpeContainerMetadata-AppOnly.ps1 in full (both already confidential-client per task 011).</step>
    <step order="1" name="Container-type provisioner">Author GraphContainerTypeProvisioner: POST /storage/fileStorage/containerTypes under ClientCertificateCredential, cert sourced from KV via SecretClient at call time.</step>
    <step order="2" name="App-only verifier">Author GraphAppOnlyContainerVerifier: the single GET, dramatically simpler than the 123-line script (no token-ceremony boilerplate needed -- ClientCertificateCredential handles it).</step>
    <step order="3" name="KV writer">Reuse task 125's SecretClient pattern for the canonical SPE-ContainerTypeId write.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Wire up">Replace the 3 collaborators in H8's owning module with the new implementations.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Tests">T6 cert-path test (confirms ClientCertificateCredential, not a secret-based credential, is used) + created/verify/24h-pending outcome tests per DS-4 §7's test-effort note.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Build + verify">dotnet build 0 errors; dotnet test green; grep 'ClientSecretCredential' in the new H8 files returns 0 matches.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the cert-based ClientCertificateCredential construction fails against the pinned Microsoft.Graph SDK version's expected certificate format (PFX vs PEM, password handling), STOP and escalate rather than falling back to a client-secret credential for expediency — that would silently violate the T6 MUST rule.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">build/test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/SpeContainerType/GraphContainerTypeProvisioner.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/SpeContainerType/GraphAppOnlyContainerVerifier.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">grep 'ClientSecretCredential' in the new H8 collaborator files returns 0 matches -- ClientCertificateCredential only.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">grep 'ProcessStartInfo' in the new H8 collaborator files returns 0 matches.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A test confirms GraphContainerTypeProvisioner constructs its Graph client with a certificate credential sourced from KV, not a secret.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A test confirms the handler correctly classifies a 24h-pending replication response as WaitingOnGate (session-free wait), not as a Fail.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build exits 0; dotnet test exits 0.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Justification (CLAUDE.md §11): Existing -- both source scripts are ALREADY confidential-client per task 011's Phase B hardening; the T6 auth model does not need re-deriving, only porting to SDK calls. Extension -- porting the already-correct auth model to Graph SDK calls under the same certificate-credential shape is the minimal correct move. Cost-of-doing-nothing -- H8 cannot execute under Option D's zero-shell main site; T6 (the confidential-client trap this handler owns) stays unverifiable by H13 (task 175) without a real handler to probe.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
